@startuml orchestrator_class
title plogic - Orchestrator stage

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

interface UI {
}

class Orchestrator {
  +{static} evaluate(source: str, simplify: bool): Result<List<TruthTable>, List<Error>>
  +{static} simplify(source: str): Result<List<str>, List<Error>>
  +{static} report(error: Error): str
}

class Token

class Scanner
class Parser
class ScanState
class ParseState
class Simplifier
class Interpreter
class TruthTable
class InfixPrinter
abstract class Expression
enum Error

note bottom of Orchestrator
  Stateless: pure composition of the pipeline
  scan -> parse -> per proposition (simplify ->
  choose expression -> interpret). Failure is always
  signalled by Result, with Err = List<Error>.

  Stage gates: a scan failure stops before parsing,
  a parse failure stops before simplification, and
  an EvalError stops the whole run. Steps 6-9 repeat
  once per parsed proposition.

  Step 8 tabulates the simplified expression by
  default, or the original with --no-simplificar.
  simplify() stops after simplification, returns the
  formula texts and builds no tables, so no size
  limit applies (--simplificar).
  evaluate() adds each table's display text through
  TruthTable.with_display: the tabulated expression in
  the label and, when simplification ran, the simplified
  formula in canonical order (InfixPrinter). report() is
  a pure formatter for the CLI. All three take their
  owned argument by value (ADR-044, ADR-046).
end note

UI --> Orchestrator

Orchestrator ..> Scanner : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Parser : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Simplifier : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Interpreter : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> TruthTable : with_display
Orchestrator ..> InfixPrinter : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Expression : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Error : <<use>>

Scanner ..> ScanState
Parser ..> ParseState
ScanState --> Token
ParseState --> Token
Interpreter ..> TruthTable : <<create>>
UI ..> TruthTable : <<use>>

@enduml
